<script type="text/javascript" src="/scripts/post_wizard.js"></script>
<div id="backoffice">
<p class="title">
 Existing Post Types:
</p>
A "post type" is just a template living in <code>templates/html/components/forms/</code>.
Every post picks exactly one of them &mdash; it's what the <em>Content Template</em> dropdown
selects when you edit a Series.
<hr />
<ul id="existing-post-types">
: for $forms -> $form {
    <li><: $form :></li>
: }
</ul>
<hr />
<p class="title">
 Create a new Post Type:
</p>
This writes a new template into the forms directory currently in use
(<code><: $forms_dir :></code>) along with a matching <code>.json</code> sidecar describing
any custom fields, so that the data model knows to keep them when a post is saved.
<hr />

<form class="Submissions" id="postTypeWizard" method="post" action="/admin/wyzzerdd/save">
    Type Name * &mdash; letters, numbers, dash and underscore only<br />
    <input required class="cooltext" type="text" name="name" pattern="[A-Za-z0-9_-]+" placeholder="recipe" value="<: $name :>" />

    <p class="title">Canned Fields</p>
    Most post types reuse the same handful of blocks.  Tick whichever ones this type needs.
    The title input, the visibility selector (visibility.tx) and the ACL selector (acls.tx)
    are always included &mdash; every post has all three, and a type whose editor cannot set
    them produces posts nobody can title, find or restrict.
    <br />
    <label for="wiz-wrapper">Wrap output in the standard post &lt;div&gt;<input id="wiz-wrapper" class="coolcb" type="checkbox" name="wrapper" value="1" <: $checked.wrapper :> /></label><br />
    <label for="wiz-post_title">Post title &amp; permalink (post_title.tx)<input id="wiz-post_title" class="coolcb" type="checkbox" name="inc_post_title" value="1" <: $checked.inc_post_title :> /></label><br />
    <label for="wiz-post_tags">Post tag list (post_tags.tx)<input id="wiz-post_tags" class="coolcb" type="checkbox" name="inc_post_tags" value="1" <: $checked.inc_post_tags :> /></label><br />
    <label for="wiz-preview">Preview image upload (preview.tx)<input id="wiz-preview" class="coolcb" type="checkbox" name="inc_preview" value="1" <: $checked.inc_preview :> /></label><br />
    <label for="wiz-tags">Tag editor (tags.tx)<input id="wiz-tags" class="coolcb" type="checkbox" name="inc_tags" value="1" <: $checked.inc_tags :> /></label><br />
    <label for="wiz-aliases">Alias URL editor (aliases.tx)<input id="wiz-aliases" class="coolcb" type="checkbox" name="inc_aliases" value="1" <: $checked.inc_aliases :> /></label><br />
    <label for="wiz-attachments">Attachment uploader (attachments.tx)<input id="wiz-attachments" class="coolcb" type="checkbox" name="inc_attachments" value="1" <: $checked.inc_attachments :> /></label><br />

    <br />
    Title placeholder text<br />
    <input class="cooltext" type="text" name="title_placeholder" placeholder="Iowa Man Destroys Moon" value="<: $title_placeholder :>" />

    <br />
    Content Body &mdash; this is always the last thing in the editor, and is what carries the post body itself.<br />
    <select class="cooltext" name="body_form">
        <option value="form_common.tx" <: $body_form == 'form_multi.tx' ? '' : 'selected' :> >Single page (form_common.tx)</option>
        <option value="form_multi.tx" <: $body_form == 'form_multi.tx' ? 'selected' : '' :> >Multiple pages, like presentations (form_multi.tx)</option>
    </select>

    <p class="title">Custom Fields</p>
    These become extra inputs in the editor, and are available in your display template below
    as <code>&lt;: $post.your_field_name :&gt;</code>.
    Uploads aren't supported here &mdash; use the Attachment uploader above for those.
    <br />
    An <em>Another Post</em> field depends on a different post type.
    <em>Pick one</em> stores a single post's ID, chosen from a dropdown in the editor, and hands you
    the whole post as <code>&lt;: $post.your_field_name_post :&gt;</code>.
    <em>All of them</em> stores nothing and simply hands you every post of that type as
    <code>&lt;: $post.your_field_name :&gt;</code> to loop over.
    <div id="wizard-params"></div>
    <button type="button" style="float:right;" class="coolbutton" onclick="addParam(); return false;">Add Field</button>
    <br style="clear:both;" />

    <p class="title">Display Template</p>
    <a href="https://metacpan.org/pod/Text::Xslate::Syntax::Kolon" title="GET UR MIND RITE">Kolon</a>
    markup for how this post type renders when someone looks at it.
    <br />
    <code>&lt;: $tiled :&gt;</code> is true when the series asked for its posts to be tiled, so branch on it
    if this type wants a compact view &mdash; see <code>forms/file.tx</code> for the shape.
    The wrapper gets the <code>tile</code> class either way.
    Note that it is only ever true for logged-out visitors: an editor needs the full view.
    Use <code>&lt;: $post.yourfield :&gt;</code> for your custom fields, and
    <code>&lt;: render_it($post.data) | mark_raw :&gt;</code> for the post body.
    <br />
    <textarea class="cooltext" name="display" rows="12" placeholder="&lt;div class=&quot;postData responsive-text&quot;&gt;&#10;    &lt;: render_it($post.data) | mark_raw :&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;"><: $display :></textarea>

    <br />
    <label for="wiz-overwrite">Overwrite it if this type already exists?<input id="wiz-overwrite" class="coolcb" type="checkbox" name="overwrite" value="1" <: $checked.overwrite :> /></label>
    <br />
    <input type="submit" class="coolbutton" value="Create Post Type" />
</form>

<template id="wizard-param-template">
    <div class="wizard-param-row">
        <hr />
        Name <input required class="cooltext" type="text" name="param_name" pattern="[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*" placeholder="cook_time" />
        Type <select class="cooltext param-type" name="param_type" onchange="syncRelationRow(this);">
            <option value="text">Text</option>
            <option value="url">URL</option>
            <option value="number">Number</option>
            <option value="date">Date</option>
            <option value="textarea">Long Text</option>
            <option value="checkbox">Checkbox</option>
            <option value="relation">Another Post</option>
        </select>
        <span class="wizard-relation" style="display:none;">
            of type <select class="cooltext" name="param_relation_form">
: for $forms -> $form {
                <option value="<: $form :>"><: $form :></option>
: }
            </select>
            <select class="cooltext" name="param_relation_mode">
                <option value="one">pick one</option>
                <option value="all">all of them</option>
            </select>
        </span>
        Label <input class="cooltext" type="text" name="param_label" placeholder="Cook Time" />
        Placeholder <input class="cooltext" type="text" name="param_placeholder" placeholder="45 minutes" />
        <select class="cooltext" name="param_required">
            <option value="0">Optional</option>
            <option value="1">Required</option>
        </select>
        <button type="button" class="coolbutton" onclick="delParam(this); return false;">Remove</button>
    </div>
</template>
</div>
